## Notes for the future executor agent

- Migration numbering is sequential and immutable. Check the highest existing migration number before creating a new file (`ls automatiklabs/supabase/migrations/ | tail -5`).
- SCHEMA-01 (enums) is a hard dependency for every subsequent migration. Always run it first in a fresh environment.
- Schema Extensions does NOT write function bodies — it owns REVOKE + GRANT EXECUTE wiring. The function bodies for `publish_lesson`, `record_competency_transition` are written by Pedagogical Workflow but placed into migration files here.
- Use `tomik-db-doctrine` skill for migration style conventions.
- Always run `supabase db reset` locally after creating a migration to verify clean apply.
